    {
      "path": "runtimes/codex/rpc-control.ts",
      "sourcePath": "packages/oar/src/runtimes/codex/rpc-control.ts",
      "upstreamSha256": "606af28dc7e85fba45a6f653e2093e8ea2c868ed7535f0021d65ab5c6455ea95",
      "vendoredSha256": "bf162859b9776946c83ceec2d9b01a5c1f40e0804fc4b3b3a4813bea0b91d53a",
      "delta": "Pass configurable control deadline (default 30000ms) and record typed RPC timeouts as rejected responses. Use an equivalent deferred Promise compatible with the SDK ES2022 lib. S2b: replace the redundant deferred response waiter with synchronous response capture to avoid hanging on required-consumer/budget failure. 0.37.0 re-vendor: keep the synchronous capture with the upstream fallback takeover, exited outcome and late-reply frame; a failed takeover record rejects the control and never escapes the fallback timer."
    },
    {
      "path": "runtimes/codex/session.ts",
      "sourcePath": "packages/oar/src/runtimes/codex/session.ts",
      "upstreamSha256": "bb9856ce96dc7348761f945086f932c99226f45289dc1c11d175bd1fe854bbf6",
      "vendoredSha256": "3e39a0550dd46967662f2d764974b0a5b761bb8025273761be4ac8a4549b79d3",
      "delta": "BYOK S2a: injected spawn and explicit filtered env; caller-selected sandbox (danger-full-access default, inherit passes no override); raw AdapterSession without sealSession/input-images; native-first frame capture with visible fold failure/kill; bounded server request decline/reject using 0.159.2 response schemas; ES2022 deferred Promise. S2b: explicit body.origin=byok-native; inject required consumer/budget before registration. Re-vendor: remove capabilities.steer; refine optional generic steer to a required Codex method; no withdraw or derived deliver. Native interactions: explicit on-request policy with readback, opt-in caller-owned request lifecycle, one-shot typed replies and local cancellation records; no fallback allow or persistence. Native replies await acknowledged stdin writes under bounded ownership. 0.33.1 re-vendor: build the open request before the owned spawn and pass its redactor to the client. 0.37.0 re-vendor: take the upstream abort fallback; its kill and the server-request deadline timer never throw out of the timer. 0.44.0 re-vendor: take the upstream input-delivery fold, steer acceptance record and MCP tool denials; options.env stays a complete string environment, so no value is a null removal; steer keeps caller-owned image admission; omit upstream resources."
    },
